From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(windows): report CPU time in time and times

On Windows the time keyword and the times builtin always reported zero
user and system time: the resource functions were stubs.  Take the
shell's own time from GetProcessTimes.  Windows has no RUSAGE_CHILDREN,
so before it starts its first child, the shell joins a new job object.
The job accounts for every process started from then on, grandchildren
and exited processes included; the shell's own time since joining is
subtracted.  Children may still break away from the job.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
